  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABEJn-9g",
      "title": "op-signer: add scoped message signing",
      "author": "wwared",
      "number": 745,
      "body": "Adds an mTLS-authorized EIP-191 message-signing RPC with exclusive method scoping, sender-based key selection, and signature/address verification for SPN requester identities. Related to https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/core-team/issues/3040.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-18T21:44:14Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 296,
      "deletions": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABDcmgMw",
      "title": "fix(cci-stats): paginate CircleCI workflow jobs",
      "author": "huklaa",
      "number": 743,
      "body": "Summary\r\n\r\nFixes #710.\r\n\r\nThe CircleCI stats collector previously processed only the first page of workflow jobs. Workflows containing more jobs than a single API response could therefore produce incomplete or inaccurate statistics.\r\n\r\nThis change:\r\n\r\n- follows CircleCI pagination until no \"next_page_token\" remains\r\n- combines jobs from every returned page\r\n- preserves the existing behavior for single-page responses\r\n- adds regression coverage for paginated workflow-job responses\r\n\r\nValidation\r\n\r\n- \"go test ./...\"\r\n- \"go vet ./...\"\r\n- \"go build ./cmd/runner\"\r\n- \"git diff --check\"",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-14T12:22:25Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 159,
      "deletions": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABEDqwlA",
      "title": "fix(proxyd): expand env vars in consensus_ha_redis.url",
      "author": "parkjeongryul",
      "number": 744,
      "body": "**Description**\n\nThe top-level `[redis].url` goes through `ReadFromEnvOrConfig`, but `consensus_ha_redis.url` is passed straight to `NewRedisClient`. Same `RedisConfig` type, different treatment — so `url = \"$REDIS_URL\"` is taken literally in the HA block, `ParseURL` chokes on it, and proxyd dies at startup. Looks like an oversight.\n\nThis adds the same call the top-level block already makes. Only `.URL` — the HA tracker doesn't read `.ReadURL`.\n\n**Tests**\n\nAdded `TestConsensusHARedisURLFromEnv` plus a `consensus_ha.toml` fixture. It starts a miniredis, exports `REDIS_URL`, and boots proxyd with `consensus_ha_redis.url = \"$REDIS_URL\"` — same setup `caching_test.go` already uses. Reverting the one-line change makes it fail with `redis: invalid URL scheme:`. Existing `TestConsensus*` still pass.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-18T09:11:10Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-18T16:14:37Z",
      "additions": 80,
      "deletions": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABDZ7Gtg",
      "title": "fix(op-conductor-mon): node_leader metric to only report with correct server ids",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 742,
      "body": "Signed-off-by: Yashvardhan Kukreja <yashvardhan@oplabs.co>\r\n\r\n<!-- Contributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n\r\n**Description**\r\n\r\nIn rare situations, op-conductor ends up returning the response to `conductor_leaderWIthID` as \"N/A (Leader Overriden)\"\r\n\r\nThe node_leader metric shouldn't be reported with such leader id. This PR fixes that.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"468\" height=\"321\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0464c1cf-4c94-4c32-aa73-bac1030be144\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nA clear and concise description of the features you're adding in this pull request.\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\nPlease describe any tests you've added. If you've added no tests, or left important behavior untested, please explain why not.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nAdd any other context about the problem you're solving.\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n- Fixes #[Link to Issue]\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-14T06:20:09Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-16T00:42:47Z",
      "additions": 78,
      "deletions": 1
    }
